## 3. Header today

  Title: Launch a pinned ingest payload.

  Logline: Re-hash the CAS blob and refuse yank, extra caps, or
  sha drift. The blob is unchanged.

  Setup: Reads lock v2 and CAS. Default is print path.
  `--exec` may run the blob.

  Beats:
    1. Find the lock node and live CAS bytes.
    2. `pm_launch_gate` must be ok or ERR and no exec.
    3. `--json` prints a machine object.
       Help does not claim transmutation.

  RULES.oot 1.7: the code must do what the document says.
  The Setup word `may` is not honest.
  The body does not run the blob.
  Beat 3 uses `transmutation`. That word is not simple.
  The CLI help in `main.oo` does not name `--exec`.

## 4. Body today

  After the gate returns ok, `--exec` runs:

    sh -c "test -e <path>; exit 0"

  `test -e` checks that the path exists.
  It does not run the pinned `.oo`.
  It does not call `run_oodac_run`.
  It does not start `oodac run`.

  The shell then runs `exit 0`.
  That discards the result of `test -e`.
  A missing path still returns success from the shell.
  `launch_die("exec")` runs only if `sys_exec` cannot start `sh`.

  After that check, the command still prints
  `ooda launch: ok <path>`.
  With `--json` it prints `"ok":true` and the path.
  The user can think the payload ran. It did not.

  Gate fail: `launch_die`. Non-zero exit.
  No `ooda launch: ok`.
  The `--exec` branch and the default branch both die.
  That refuse path is honest.

## 5. Required meaning

  `--exec` must mean run, not exists.

  After the gate returns ok, `--exec` must run the pinned `.oo`.
  Use the same path as `ooda run <payload>` (`run_oodac_run`).
  The child must be the payload, not `test -e`.

  Without `--exec`, print the path only.
  Do not start `oodac`.
  Do not print payload stdout.
  Do not print `LAUNCH_EXEC_OK`.

  Gate fail stays fail-closed.
  Non-zero exit.
  No payload process.
  No `ooda launch: ok`.

  `--json` plus `--exec` must not print `"ok":true` before the
  child finishes.
  If the child fails, do not print ok.

## 6. What must stay

  Re-hash the live CAS bytes against the lock sha.
  Refuse yank, extra caps, and sha drift.
  The blob stays unchanged. No rewrite. No transcode.

  `cli/pm_launch.oo` already says: re-check sha256, cap subset,
  and yank before any exec. Keep that order.
  Prefer no edit to the gate file.

  Public `registry/hello/hello.oo` has `hello_ok`.
  It has no `pub fn main`.
  Do not change it.
  Do not treat `hello_ok` as a program.

  Do not grow `ooda/pm/`.
  Product is `cli/`.
  Ship 2 does not edit `cli/main.oo`.

## 7. Header DE1 must write

  After the body runs the pinned `.oo`, the header must match.
  Do not keep `may`.
  Do not keep `transmutation`.
  Do not say existence check.

  Required sense (ASD-STE100):

    Logline: Re-hash the CAS blob and refuse yank, extra caps,
    or sha drift. Then print the path, or run the pinned `.oo`
    when `--exec` is set.

    Setup: Reads lock v2 and CAS. Default prints the path.
    `--exec` runs the pinned `.oo` after the gate.
    Without `--exec` the command does not run the file.

    Beats:
      1. Find the lock node and live CAS bytes.
      2. `pm_launch_gate` must be ok or ERR and no exec.
      3. After ok, `--exec` runs the pinned `.oo`.
         Without `--exec`, print the path only.

  The Academy header is the help surface for this ship.
  `main.oo` is locked to ship 3.
  Do not add a launch line there from this worktree.

## 8. Public site (do not edit)

  This wave does not touch `openOODA.github.io/`.

  `guide/Options.oot`: `--exec` runs it after sha, caps, and
  yank checks. That sentence is false on disk today.
  It becomes true only after this ship.

  `guide/Packages.oot`: `--exec` runs after the gate. Then:
  the `--exec` step is an existence check after that gate.
  Those two sentences do not agree.

  `guide/Safety.oot`: `--exec` checks that the CAS path exists
  after sha, caps, and yank are ok. That matches today's body.
  It will be false after a real run lands.

  A later owner pass must make the three pages say one thing:
  `--exec` runs the pinned `.oo` after the gate.
  Without `--exec`, print the path only.
  Do not write that pass now.

## 9. Proof words for later smokes

  HARN owns the new fixture and smoke.
  DOCS only names the words the header and smoke must share.

  Without `--exec`:
    stdout has `ooda launch: ok` and the CAS path.
    stdout does not have `LAUNCH_EXEC_OK`.

  With `--exec` on the new fixture:
    stdout has `LAUNCH_EXEC_OK`.
    The child is `oodac run` on the pinned `.oo`.

  Hostile yank, sha drift, extra caps, and a bad name:
    stdout has `ERR`.
    stdout does not have `LAUNCH_EXEC_OK`.
    stdout does not have `ooda launch: ok`.

  A smoke that only greps `test -e` out of source is not proof.
  SK1 will require the fixture output.

